Real failure output from this build, for comparison against your own.
Lenovo Legion 5 15IAX10 + Razer Core X V2 (USB4), RTX 5070 Laptop 8GB + RTX 5060 Ti 16GB.

================================================================================
1. THE DRIVER VERSION COLLISION
================================================================================

Get-CimInstance Win32_PnPSignedDriver -Filter "DeviceClass='DISPLAY'"

  DeviceName    : NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Ti
  DriverVersion : 32.0.15.9186          -> 591.86
  DriverDate    : 20/01/2026
  InfName       : oem268.inf            (original: nv_dispig.inf, desktop)

  DeviceName    : NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Laptop GPU
  DriverVersion : 32.0.16.1692          -> 616.92
  DriverDate    : 09/04/2026
  InfName       : oem277.inf            (original: nvlti.inf, notebook)

Two packages, two versions, one nvlddmkm.sys. Only one GPU can work.


================================================================================
2. DEVICE STATES WHILE BROKEN
================================================================================

Hot-plugged, both cards present:

  NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Ti          Error   CM_PROB_NORMAL_CONFLICT   (Code 12)
  Intel(R) Graphics                   OK      CM_PROB_NONE
  NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Laptop GPU  Error   CM_PROB_FAILED_ADD        (Code 31)

  nvidia-smi: Failed to initialize NVML: Not Found

After a cold boot with the enclosure attached, the failure swapped cards:

  NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Ti          OK      CM_PROB_NONE
  NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Laptop GPU  Error   CM_PROB_FAILED_ADD        (Code 31)

  0, NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Ti, 591.86, 16311 MiB, 00000000:06:00.0

That swap is the tell: resource contention does not ping-pong between devices.


================================================================================
3. NVIDIA INSTALLER FAILING WITH A LIVE GPU  (C:\Windows\INF\setupapi.dev.log)
================================================================================

Running setup.exe -s -clean -noreboot with the eGPU connected:

  inf:  Service 'nvlddmkm' still in use by 2 sources.
  cpy:  Skipping isolated file 'nvlddmkm.sys'.
  idb:  {Unpublish Driver Package: C:\Windows\System32\DriverStore\FileRepository\
          nvlti.inf_amd64_c284234d5322c92e\nvlti.inf}
  idb:  Unregistered driver package 'nvlti.inf_amd64_c284234d5322c92e' from 'oem277.inf'.

It removed the working package FIRST, then failed to copy the replacement.
Result: RTX 5070 dropped to Code 28, "drivers for this device are not installed".

With the eGPU disconnected instead, the desktop installer refused to run at all:

  installer exit code: -469762016   (0xE4000020)


