================================================================================
5. ENCLOSURE NOT ON THE BUS  (wrong cable)
================================================================================

Plugging in produced ZERO device events. Not an error - nothing at all:

  Get-WinEvent ... StartTime <marker>
    DistributedCOM  10010
    HttpService       114
    (no PnP, no USB, no USB4 events)

  USB4(TM) Host Router (Microsoft)        OK        <- laptop controller fine
  USB4 Router (2.0), Razer - Core X V2    Unknown   <- enclosure not enumerated

Cause: a USB-C cable carrying power and USB 2.0 only. Physically identical to a
USB4 cable. With the correct cable the router went to OK immediately.


================================================================================
6. LM STUDIO / llama.cpp OUT OF MEMORY
================================================================================

  W common_fit_params: failed to fit params to free device memory:
      n_gpu_layers already set by user to 999999, abort
  E ggml_backend_cuda_buffer_type_alloc_buffer: allocating 5830.00 MiB on device 1:
      cudaMalloc failed: out of memory
  E alloc_tensor_range: failed to allocate CUDA1 buffer of size 6113198080
  E llama_init_from_model: failed to initialize the context:
      failed to allocate buffer for kv cache

  srv load_model: initializing, n_slots = 4, n_ctx_slot = 262144, kv_unified = 'true'

Note: "device 1" / "CUDA1" proves multi-GPU IS working. The failure is capacity,
specifically the KV cache, amplified 4x by n_slots = 4.
